.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt USERDEL 8
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm userdel
.Nd remove a user
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl prv
.Ar user
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility removes
.Ar user
from the account database, in the shape of the
.Nx
and
.Ox
command.
It is
.Xr pw 8
under another name.
The user is also removed from every group's member list, its crontab
is removed, and so is its own group (named like it) if no other user
has that group as its primary group.
The superuser account
.Ql root
cannot be removed.
It must be run by the superuser.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl p
Preserve the account but make it unusable: the password is locked and
the shell set to
.Pa /sbin/nologin .
.It Fl r
Also remove the home directory and the mail spool.
A home directory is only removed if it is a directory the user owns
that no other account uses.
.It Fl v
Say what was done.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
As
.Xr pw 8 .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pw 8 ,
.Xr rmuser 8 ,
.Xr useradd 8 ,
.Xr usermod 8
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
utility appeared in
.Nx 1.5
and
.Ox 2.7 .
This implementation was written for OxideBSD.
